# Netlify Redirects Configuration
# This file tells Netlify to serve index.html for all routes
# allowing React Router to handle client-side routing

# Redirect all routes to index.html with 200 status (SPA fallback)
/*    /index.html   200

# Alternative: If you need to handle specific API routes differently
# /api/*  https://your-backend-api.com/api/:splat  200

# Note: The 200 status code is important - it serves index.html
# without changing the URL, allowing React Router to work correctly
